      "text": "**Yes—given your asthma, I’d keep outdoor time to a minimum in KL today, especially exercise.** Recent reports put readings around **API 160–163** at some KL-area stations—within Malaysia’s “unhealthy” range, though readings vary by location and hour. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/wp-kuala-lumpur?utm_source=openai))\n\nYou don’t necessarily need to stay inside all day: keep trips brief and easy, avoid strenuous activity, and check the latest reading for your area before heading out. Keep your reliever inhaler with you and follow your asthma action plan. Air pollution can affect people with asthma even when they’re indoors, so keep windows closed if the air outside seems hazy. ([epa.gov](https://www.epa.gov/pmcourse/patient-exposure-and-air-quality-index?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you’re wheezing or short of breath, go indoors and use your action plan; seek urgent medical help if breathing becomes severe or your reliever isn’t helping.",
